regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_minimax.txt:27:**The first-call `v0` result is not asserted.** `v0_after1` is captured and feeds the `v0 read` control row (regex matched), but its value is never compared to anything. A fix that returns the old context correctly on the *second* call but returns something wrong on the *first* call would pass all four rows. For a one-line fix that does not branch on call count this is implausible, but it is a real gap on paper.
regress\artifacts\gdromcondlies\postfix_20260830\README.md:28:Four rows flipped, and they are exactly the kill rows. Columns are **`got want`** —
regress\artifacts\alphaswpctxreg\pass2_panel_20260908\ollama_kimi.txt:14:**Q4 — it separates its two named hypotheses, and yes, there is a third.** (REASONED) "Handler never ran" → a0 = N; "ran, wrong register" → a0 = C; that part holds. The unconsidered third: `old ctx == C` is *inferred*, never observed — it assumes call 1's `ctx = a0` install worked on the broken build, and the only post-install observation is `a0 land` itself. A `print a0` after call 1 (pre-fix: would show initial ctx, not C) is a free independent falsifier the probe declines to collect. Note also `a0 land` alone cannot distinguish "correct no-clobber" from "call 2 never ran" post-fix — the `v0 ctx` row covers it, so the ensemble is sound, but the control is not load-bearing solo.
