regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\pass2_01a0339\ollama_glm.txt:15:Sign-guard side: the live candidate is **keep the guard, delete `x |= ~mask`** (equivalently `x |= 0`). It is value-visible exactly when a field's top bit is SET at width < 32. Against every named row it is GREEN: `s clear` → 0x7 *requires no* extension; `s w31` → 0x09abcdef *requires no* extension; `s w32` → 0x89abcdef is green and **provably blind — at width 32 extension is the identity `x |= 0`, so the row looks like it exercises extension (field top bit SET) but cannot**; UBFX rows never extend. So the mutant sweeps every row inlined in this packet. I can name 11 of the 14 rows; the other three decide it. **Not checkable; settling fact: does any shipped row expect an SBFX result exceeding its field mask at width < 32 (e.g. 0xffffffde from SBFX #4,#8)?** Or measure: run the 14-row probe against `x |= ~mask` deleted. If 14/14 — L2 breach; the in-round repair is a must-extend row: SBFX #4,#8 of 0x89abcdef gives field 0xde, bit 7 SET → 0xffffffde (mirrors `mid`; green under shipped code and always-extend; failure value 0xde ≠ 0, so it needs no pc companion). Note this is **not** the disclosed topBitMask escape — that is definedness; this is value coverage, and the `ubsanshiftlane` filing does not cover it.
