regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:940:So the guest-observation claim: REASONED, valid under the named lowering (x86-family count-mod-32); the brief correctly labels it as a lowering-dependent guess. I add: it is not just a guess about the host ISA — it's also a guess about the compiler (a compiler could recognize the pattern... unlikely with runtime values). The single settling measurement: run UBFX #0,#32 on the project's actual build on its actual host and read rd — the brief declines to build the witness; fine. The measurement to name: a UBSan-instrumented build executing `UBFX rd, rn, #0, #32` (and #31) — would trap on both widths. That's the "measurement not inlined" to name.
