regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\codex_fixcheck_20260907.txt:44:| **Decline during decode; potentially halt** — 3 decisions | ARM `X(to_be_translated)` sends [MSR using PC](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:4146), [MOVW to PC, and MOVT to PC](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:4279) to `bad`. The included [cpu_dyntrans.c translation tail](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_dyntrans.c:1983) merely returns during read-ahead; during execution it diagnoses the failure and sets `cpu->running = 0`. Thus decode rejection alone does not specify a guest outcome. **Diagnose and stop emulation is a fifth member.** |
regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\codex_fixcheck_20260907.txt:46:| **Decline an optimization or defer execution** — 3 decisions | [ARM `COMBINE(strlen)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:3521) rejects the fold while preserving ordinary instruction execution. [MIPS `X(beq)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_instr.c:182) and [SH `X(bra)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c:2241) defer nested delayed branches for subsequent normal execution. These are additional responses beyond your four. |
