regress\artifacts\armbfxwidth32\codex_armcapability_20260907.txt:43:**`#312` fixes one particular decoder fallback.** On actual execution it installs `cond_instr(und)` and records the instruction’s page offset. `arm_instr_und()` synchronizes PC and calls `arm_exception(ARM_EXCEPTION_UND)`. Consequently, the exception occurs only when the instruction’s condition passes. Read-ahead merely declines translation; non-permanently-undefined extension cases receive a warning once. This is not universal undefined routing for every unsupported encoding. See [the corrected branch](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:4495) and [`arm_instr_und()`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_instr.c:1020).
