regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\SELFREVIEW_brief.md:81:**Q5. Scope.** You listed `lca_ioc`'s default arm, the two interrupt handlers and `lca_isa`'s guard
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\FIX_brief.md:111:3. **Is IMPLEMENT even the right member here?** The alternatives: DECLINE the cycle silently;
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\FIX_brief.md:112:   DECLINE with a latched announce; or return all-ones explicitly without touching `bus_pci`. Note
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\FIX_brief.md:125:   and `lca_interrupt_assert`/`_deassert` are still bare kills (filed as `lcairqstubkill`, witnessed).
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\ollama_minimax.txt:9:**Q3 — IMPLEMENT vs alternatives.** REASONED. IMPLEMENT is the only member that degrades correctly if a device is ever placed on bus 1. DECLINE / latched-announce / explicit-all-ones are observationally identical today (empty bus, all-ones) but would silently mis-route a real bus-1 device. The defect closes either way; IMPLEMENT is the honest member.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\ollama_minimax.txt:11:**Q4 — the discriminating row.** REASONED. `0xffffffffffffffff` on the armed read separates IMPLEMENT / explicit-all-ones from any DECLINE variant (which would read as 0). It does **not** separate IMPLEMENT from explicit-all-ones — both return all-ones on an empty bus. To split them, place a synthetic device on bus 1 and probe it: IMPLEMENT would read the device's actual config; explicit-all-ones would still return all-ones. Not possible without a fixture. The row is best-available; record the conflation as a known limit, not a defect in the witness.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\ollama_minimax.txt:13:**Q5 — not closed.** READ from brief. `default:` arm of `lca_ioc` and `lca_interrupt_{assert,deassert}` are separate kills, untouched by this fix.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:78:### Q3 — IMPLEMENT (member 7). Decline is a lie at vendor ID.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:84:| silent decline / `return 1` without writing | `0` (`memory_rw.c` `#95` pre-zero) |
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:89:PCI ID probes treat `0xffffffff` as “absent” and `0` as “vendor 0”. Decline that returns 0 can invent a device. The house idiom in all 10 `bus_pci_setaddr` callers is decode-and-dispatch, not decline.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:110:1. **Survival** of the armed access (the witness already has this; it greens silent decline, latched announce, and IMPLEMENT alike).
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:115:Still conflated after that: IMPLEMENT vs “decline that forges the same two values”; `bus = ioc_conf&1` vs `bus` from the tag, on any empty secondary bus. Disclose both. Do not add a `bus_pci_add(..., 1, …)` to alphabook1 to pin them — that is a product topology change, not a detector row.
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:126:- `lca_interrupt_assert` / `_deassert` (`lcairqstubkill`).
regress\artifacts\lcaconfbus1kill\pass1_panel\grok.txt:139:3. **`i82378zb` is `PCI_SUBCLASS_BRIDGE_ISA`**, header type 0, multifunction (`PCIINIT(i82378zb)`). A well-behaved guest will probably never write `IOC_CONF=1` on this machine. The kill is still guest-drivable; the witness did it in two instructions. That does not licence DECLINE.
