regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_implement_v2_20260908.txt:31:My implementation inference is that the **minimum useful callback repair** is an upstream `struct interrupt` stored in `lca_data`, connected during initialization to `devinit->interrupt_path`, with assert/deassert forwarding the corresponding level. The [default path already names the bootstrap CPU](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/device.c:278).
regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_implement_v2_20260908.txt:43:- Footbridge registers `interrupt->line` as a **bit mask**. LCA registers the **index zero**. Copying `status |= interrupt->line` would record nothing.
