regress\artifacts\pass2_79cd12e\seats\ollama_glm.txt:25:**Found, not zero.** One candidate is clean on the packet's own account: the DEVINIT exit mutant above — it is in the walked-to-boundary dominator set of an edited line, and by the comment's own account (measured at `-n 5`, both ways — READ, not re-measured here) no accepted configuration can observe it. If the panel accepts it, that is the L2 breach, and it exposes an unrecorded conflict: the repair the floor demands (the clamp) is exactly what the addition licence refuses without a measured delta. Two further families (label/flag deletions; gate mutants) are clean **iff** the probes are as sparse as their named rows — that is a zero-looked-for hole, not a zero-found, and the settling fact for both is the two probes' row tables (driven vectors and asserted observables). Also recorded as a pin-gap, not a defect: the seven VERBOSITY_ERROR→INFO edits are observable to no named row.
