regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_fix_20260907.txt:9:   The minimal **wiring implementation** would give `lca_data` a connected upstream `struct interrupt`, connect it to `devinit->interrupt_path`, and forward both levels through it. That parent path already defaults to the bootstrap CPU in `device_add()`; LCA currently stores no upstream interrupt connection. ([device.c, `device_add()`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/device.c:278), [dev_lca.c, `lca_data`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c:51))
regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_fix_20260907.txt:55:   PIC IRR readback is insufficient: `isa_interrupt_assert()` updates it before invoking LCA, so both dropping variants retain that observable. ([bus_isa.c, `isa_interrupt_assert()`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/bus_isa.c:98))
regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_fix_20260907.txt:65:   PIC register operations also drive this endpoint: `dev_8259_access()` recalculates and asserts/deasserts its connected output on mask changes and EOI operations; `bus_isa_init()` connects the primary PIC directly to LCA. The reachability is broader than peripheral callbacks through `isa_interrupt_common()`. ([dev_8259.c, `dev_8259_access()`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_8259.c:103), [bus_isa.c, `bus_isa_init()`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/bus_isa.c:219))
regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_fix_20260907.txt:67:   PCI routing is unfinished separately: `DEVINIT(lca)` passes three TODO interrupt-path strings to `bus_pci_init()`. `PCIINIT(i82378zb)` advertises PIRQ assignments through configuration bytes but creates no interrupt connections. Fixing the ISA callbacks would not complete PCI interrupt routing. ([dev_lca.c, `DEVINIT(lca)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c:343), [bus_pci.c, `PCIINIT(i82378zb)`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/bus_pci.c:753))
