regress\artifacts\lcairqstubkill\codex_reach_20260907.txt:63:- `isa_interrupt_assert` records the device request in PIC IRR state. `isa_interrupt_common` cascades unmasked secondary requests onto primary IRQ2, applies masks, records `last_int`, and calls the upstream interrupt. Here that upstream handler is **`lca_interrupt_assert`, which prints its TODO diagnostic and calls `exit(1)`**. `lca_interrupt_deassert` does the same. Thus an assertion that propagates upstream terminates there; these handlers contain no CPU interrupt delivery. [bus_isa.c:52](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/bus_isa.c:52), [assert entry:98](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/bus_isa.c:98), [dev_lca.c:70](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_lca.c:70)
