regress\artifacts\sgimtedepth4dead\codex_audit_20260907.txt:3082:3. **A declined source GET still causes a destination PUT.** The helper returns without changing `bg` for invalid coordinates or an invalid tile pointer. The caller then writes `bg` anyway. Initially that is the background register; after a successful GET it is the previous source value. This is an independent stale-data corruption defect, and correcting the depth condition does not remove it. See the [helper’s early returns](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:199) and [dependent PUT](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1358).
