regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass7_panel_20260906_113427\ollama_glm.txt:1:{"model": "glm-5.3", "created_at": "2026-09-06T16:40:30.3772371Z", "response": "", "thinking": "Let me carefully parse this brief. It's a \"packet-fed seat\" review \u2014 I must reason from the inlined text alone, no file access. I need to:\n\n1. Verdict line first: CLOSE THE CHAIN / ONE MORE REPAIR / DO NOT SHIP.\n2. Answer the one question: does a clean-sweep mutant exist in the (d) enumeration of the shipped composite? If none, CLOSE with my own denominator.\n3. Answer the second question: of the pass-7 dispositions (five row closures, one channel, one disclosure withdrawn (class 10), one gate repair, one interval wording, the deepseek 0..3 class kept disclosed), WHICH IS WRONG?\n4. Label claims READ or REASONED. Never MEASURED.\n\nLet me digest the technical content.\n\nThe setup: GXemul MC88100 exception delivery. The function `m88k_exception()` has:\n- switch 1: class -> `implemented`\n- fallback: `if (vector < 128 && !implemented)` -> print `unimplemented vector=0x%03x`, stop all cpus, return\n- SFRZ re-route: `if (PSR & SFRZ) { if (!is_trap) { vector = ERROR; fatal(\"[ SFRZ already set in PSR => ERROR ]\\n\"); } update_shadow_regs = false; }`\n- common path\n- tail switch (labels per class; default prints `internal error` and stops cpu)\n\nThe probe plants `br .` at every vector entry in VECTORS, handler words at `8 * handler_at`, breakpoint at expected entry, `continue`. Result categories: HALT (fallback diagnostic naming the row's vector AND `All machines stopped.`), TAILHALT (`internal error` + stopped), STOP (anything else), BADREGS (entry bp fired but shadow/PSR/dest assert failed; bad=refatal = the re-route diagnostic present where exemption should hold or absent where re-route fired; bad=level = `exception <CLASS>` at ERROR level).\n\nThe repair diff v8 -> v10 adds:\n- Row `trapfrozen10`: frozen tb1 naming 10 enters switch 1 as ERROR class (no other row does that; err* rows