regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:9:- **P5 — READ.** Both precedents decline the rejected write (RCR1 by moving the store, `#443` by restore). Neither lets a rejected value stay resident.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:27:- **`LCA_IOC_CONF` → B.** Deciding fact, in the packet (as stated): `bus = d->ioc_conf & 1;`. Honest dependency: this inherits P2; if the consumer were wrong, CONF joins the five. Cost worth weighing: B declines whole writes, so `0x3` discards a legitimate bit-0 request; MASK (store `idata & 1`, announce the rest) avoids that but changes readback policy (P3) and has no precedent here. #447 chose whole-write decline for exactly this shape.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_p1_20260907\ollama_glm.txt:28:- **The other five — NOT SETTLEABLE from this packet.** The one fact: the scoped no-consumer grep (P2 caveat above). If it holds: accept, keep the store, keep a once-latched downgraded announce — hardware fidelity is the tiebreak the author names, and no hardware declines these writes. If the panel will not re-verify the count, B-uniform is the fact-free default. Either way, land the per-arm rationale in the tree the way #447 did, so the exemption (if taken) is explicit policy, not a silent one.
