regress\artifacts\m88kexcdeliver\pass7_panel_20260906_113427\kimi.txt:565:  Q2 answer: the trapfrozen10 row closure is the wrong disposition — it closes M_ERRORFRZOFF (the SFRZ-set polarity) but the docstring/contract treats codex's pass-6 cell ("switch 1's ERROR arm is its own predicate") as closed; the opposite polarity sweeps. The other nine dispositions check out (five... wait, trapfrozen10 IS one of the five row closures; so: of the five row closures, trapfrozen10's is wrong; the other four rows, the refatal channel, the withdrawal, the gate repair, the interval wording, and the 0..3 disclosure all verified). Count: ten dispositions, one wrong.
