regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_20260908\ollama_deepseek.txt:20:**REASONED:** The common theme: stop terminating the process on guest writes. Use the house style `(once)` decline for unsupported values, and accept/store values the manual or existing code already treats as legal.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_20260908\ollama_deepseek.txt:22:- `LCA_IOC_CONF`: **accept with backing storage** when `idata & ~1 == 0`; otherwise **decline once**.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_20260908\ollama_deepseek.txt:23:- `LCA_IOC_TB_ENA`: **accept with backing storage** when `idata & ~IOC_TB_ENA_TEN == 0`; otherwise **decline once**.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_20260908\ollama_deepseek.txt:24:- `LCA_IOC_W_BASE0`: **accept with backing storage** for the two values already accepted (`0` and `0x300800000`); otherwise **decline once**. The manual does not enumerate legal base values, so do not expand the set without evidence.
regress\artifacts\lcabadval\panel_20260908\ollama_deepseek.txt:25:- `LCA_IOC_W_MASK0`: **accept with backing storage** for all 13 legal field values, i.e. `(idata & 0xfffff) == 0` and `f = idata >> 20` satisfies `(f & (f+1)) == 0`; otherwise **decline once**. If lower bits are later found to be ignored, drop the lower-bits check.
