regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:24:That is why survival is the right **pre-fix** channel, and also why it is not enough: it is the channel the repair then destroys as a discriminator. After the check is gone, decline, accept, delete-the-check, and `return 0` all leave the host alive.
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\grok_witness_20260907.txt:52:The zero trap: GENCTL resets to `0x00`. An unmapped read also returns `0`. A post-fix “readback 0 means declined” row is the alpha-harness failure mode. Preset `0x82` (or `0x10`, which `acc all` already stores), *then* write `0x04`. Decline leaves `0x82`; accept/delete-check leaves `0x04`.
