regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass4_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:111:    LEN2: `len == 2` declines halfword, lets word land → latch all w drops. W column everywhere. SCCERR: "SCCERR's own word rows (wrd/wwr sccerr) are its S" — wait, SCCERR LEN2 is marked S, and the note says its word rows are its S. Hmm, but wwr sccerr dcl expects a decline for a word write; with LEN2 (`len == 2`) at SCCERR, word write lands (stores 0, value-identical), so wwr sccerr dcl count drops to 0 → red. Yes caught.
