regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass4_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:135:    Now the E cell: SCCERR FALL = E, warrant "the arm stores 0 and nothing in the model ever stores a nonzero SCCERR". Verify: SCCERR write body is `d->pcctwo_reg[PCCTWO_SCCERR] = 0`? Premise 5 says SCCERR's write body is `= 0`. If the arm stores 0 regardless of idata, then decline vs land → same stored state. But: does the landed write have OTHER observables? The fall-through at SCCERR: guard announces (DECL printed once), then body stores 0. Decline path: announces, breaks, stores nothing — but SCCERR reg is presumably always 0 anyway since nothing stores nonzero. So states identical. One subtlety: is there a print in the SCCERR body (HUH)? Premise 5 says "`= 0' and nothing in the model stores a nonzero SCCERR" — no HUH mentioned. If no HUH, E holds. Should verify in source.
