regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass4_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:149:    `acc all`: 12 guest st.b of 0x10, expects 0 declines. Benign inflation: DECL appears only from decline announces. st.b at GENCTL with 0x10 — GENCTL body: stores byte, reassert. 0x10 & 0x04 = 0 → no c040 kill. VECBASE st.b 0x10: stores 0x10 & 0xf0 = 0x10; idata & ~0xf0 = 0 → no HUH. PSCALEADJ st.b 0x10: body prints "ignored (value...)" — does that print contain DECL? "PSCALEADJ ignored" — no "declined" substring. OK. SCCERR st.b: stores 0. IPL st.b 0x10: writeflag==MEM_WRITE body → prints "write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL; ignored" once — contains "ignored" not DECL. OK. MASK st.b: stores, reassert — GENCTL is... in acc all session, GENCTL got 0x10 (bit 0x04 clear) → reassert from MASK write reads GENCTL 0x10 → no kill. Good. TxCTL st.b 0x10: reg = 0 | (0x10 & 3) = 0; idata & ~7 = 0x10 → HUH print "HUH? write to PCCTWO_TxCTL with value 0x10" — contains "HUH", not DECL. OK. TxICR st.b 0x10: &= ~0x17, |= 0x10 & 0x17 = 0x10; idata & 0xe0 = 0 → no HUH; reassert. SCCICR st.b 0x10: stores 0x10 & 0x1f = 0x10, reassert. SCCTX 0x1f? no — acc all uses r5=0x10 for ALL blocks. SCCTX st.b 0x10: stores byte? SCCTX body — premise doesn't detail; "SCCTX stores byte and reassert"? Premise 5 says GENCTL and MASK store the byte and reassert; SCCTX body not stated. Hmm. SCCTX is "SCC Tx" — whatever; the row measured green on BASE.
