regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass4_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:1274:  And: could a mutant move the width decline AFTER the body (decline-then-store reorder)? That's FALL-with-announce-after: stores then announces... rows: rb rows check value (unchanged — body ran? no wait, if decline is AFTER the body, the body RUNS first → write lands → rb rows red ✓ same as FALL). Covered by FALL channels.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass4_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:1302:  **Q1(d) cardinality rows.** No benign inflation: the warn text is "WARNING: address isn't aligned" (no DECL substring, `debugger_cmds.c:1514`); declined writes never reach bodies so no HUH in `latch all`; `acc all`'s byte bodies print "ignored"/"HUH"/read-only texts, none containing DECL, and 0x10 keeps `PCC2_C040`(0x04) clear everywhere — consistent with measured BASE 96/96 in part 3b/3c. Mutant-preservation: yes — the Q2 edit above preserves all three counts while breaking the property; that is the hole.
