regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\FIXDESIGN_brief.md:160:The adjudicated disposition (codex, assess stage) is **DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE**.  The option-set
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\FIXDESIGN_brief.md:208:**NOT a detector of the repair**: "host survives" greens for a silent decline, a latched decline and
regress\artifacts\sgirekills\audit_20260830\brief.md:82:declines safely while an **8-byte read still ends the host process**. Is splitting these into
regress\artifacts\sgirekills\audit_20260830\brief.md:90:delete / decline / decline + bounded-announce / **ACCEPT** (where the model already computes
regress\artifacts\sgirekills\audit_20260830\brief.md:94:path — so a read could plausibly return what was written, which would be ACCEPT, not decline.
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:1:**VERDICT: DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE for unsupported C040 delivery. Survival is a nonvacuous oracle here, but cannot establish interrupt correctness.**
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:24:**Q1:** Choose DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE **for the unsupported interrupt-delivery operation**. The register write has already been accepted; describe that distinction explicitly.
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:26:The idiom exists in this file’s `pcc2_width_decline()` and, more directly, in `dev_sgi_re.c`: per-instance warning state, latched `fatal()`, then an unconditional return outside the warning latch. `fatal()` itself is a printing function here. [PCC2 idiom](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_pcc2.c:404), [helper-return idiom](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:259), [logger](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/debugmsg.c:384).
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:31:| DECLINE, silent | Conceals an unsupported mode that can prevent guest interrupt handling. |
regress\artifacts\pcc2c040kill\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:32:| **DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE** | Makes the limitation visible while bounding repeated diagnostics from ticks and callbacks. |
