regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:5:Domain first (REASONED from the packet's premises): the producer emits len ∈ {1, 2, 4}; guest len-2 reaches even offsets only, guest len-4 only 4-aligned offsets (so among the twelve, only SCCERR 0x1c is guest-word-reachable); the operator path emits any len at any offset. Probe len-4 rows exist **only at SCCERR** (READ, gate list: `wrd/wwr/val w sccerr`), which drives several equivalences below.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:12:- **S1 delete:** M at GENCTL, MASK, TxICR; TxCTL/SCCTX equivalent to their measured S2 (no len-4 rows there, so delete ≡ len>2 for every probed access); SCCERR covered by `hwr sccerr dcl` under both (S2 measured); A at VECBASE/PSCALEADJ/SCCICR/SCCRX/SCSIICR/IPL via dcl + latch all, a mechanism measured at T1ICR (odd, operator) and MASK.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:15:  - **IPL (determined).** Delete the `break` after the decline: the announce fires (`hwr ipl dcl` = 1, green), the body prints "write to read-only PCCTWO_IPL; ignored" once and **stores nothing** (READ -- the arm is inlined). No row counts that string (`hwr ipl dcl` counts "write to PCCTWO_IPL " + DECL; the ignored line says "read-only"). All IPL rows green. PSCALEADJ's body is print-only too, and the panel built `op pscale noig` for precisely this shape -- the repair is asymmetric against its own Section-5 precedent.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:16:  - **SCCERR (determined given the packet's own warrant).** No `rb sccerr` row exists; its channels are dcl and survival, both invariant when the announce is kept; the landed write is value-identical ("always 0", PRETABLE Section 2, READ). Even `val w sccerr` must expect the unchanged 0 (it is green on BASE, where the wide write is declined). Section 5's own sentence -- "a `dcl` row cannot vary under a mutant that keeps announcing, so it was the WRONG channel" -- applies verbatim.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:17:  - **VECBASE (conditional).** `rb vecbase`'s halfword goes through GENCTL's arm at 0x02 (READ, its own note: "the second lane of the declined halfword"), so it never exercises VECBASE's guard; `op vecbase` checks survival only; no row reads VECBASE after a wide write to 0x03. Sweeps unless VECBASE's write body kills the host -- and its body is **not inlined**.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:23:REASONED, on packet facts: the session is twelve `put h` commands and nothing else -- no guest program runs; the only writer of `d->warned` is `pcc2_width_decline` (PRETABLE field audit, deriver given: one `warned |=` occurrence). (i) No benign traffic exists to pre-set a bit, and nothing else can. (ii) Twelve puts, one per arm; a shared bit yields at most 11 announce events; a repeated put could not announce anyway (latch). Both directions are READ: 12 on BASE, 11 under M1. One scoping caveat: the row detects duplicated member *use*, not permutations (a transposed pair still counts 12) -- but a permutation is behaviorally vacuous, each block still latching once on a distinct bit, so it is not a hole.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:31:Correct on the fix, enumerated: st.b 0x1f survives both masks (0x1f & 0x1f = 0x1f; 0x1f & 0xdf = 0x1f); no HUH (0x1f & ~mask = 0 both); the put h is declined; ld.bu reads 0x1f. READ-corroborated: green in both 82/82 BASE runs. Under M_FALL the landed values are 0x18 and 0x98 (enumerated: 0xb8 & 0x1f = 0x18; 0xb8 & 0xdf = 0x98), HUH fires and returns, then reassert. Whether the row then records a wrong value or "died" is **not distinguishable from the packet** -- pass 3c gives counts only. REASONED: alive with a wrong readback, because these sessions never set GENCTL's C040 bit (the same fact the `rb mask` comment leans on). The settling fact: the per-row pass-3c output for the M_FALL runs. Coverage is unaffected either way.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:35:**Delete one `break;` -- the one after `pcc2_width_decline` in the IPL arm.** One token; every row stays green (case made in 1(a)). The row I expect to stay green, and that most looks like coverage: **`hwr ipl dcl`** (still 1 -- the announce is kept). The same deletion at SCCERR and VECBASE also sweeps; at VECBASE the landed write puts a real byte into a live register with no row observing it -- there the damning green row is **`rb vecbase`**, which Section 2 credits as VECBASE's readback but which exercises GENCTL's arm. The missing rows are cheap mirrors of existing ones: an "hwr ipl noig" counting "read-only PCCTWO_IPL" == 0 (green on the fix by construction), and an own-arm readback or ruling at SCCERR/VECBASE. Outside the six shapes: **`len != 1` → `len == 2`** accepts len-4 accesses, and len-4 rows exist only at SCCERR (READ), so it sweeps at the other eleven blocks -- guest-unreachable there (alignment), but the operator path the contract claims to cover can emit it.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_glm.txt:43:Mostly yes -- and specifically: the driver death at the 10th mutant is disclosed with the 9 standing; every table names its denominator; md5 freezes are named; the NOROW line declines a claim; and premise 6 (fatal returns) is corroborated in-packet (`hwr t2ctl` stays green under M_LENGT2_TXCTL despite the HUH fatal). The defects:
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:1:**VERDICT: DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE is justified, with an unconditional return from the PUT default. But the brief misstates #504’s oracle and the write’s byte count; depth 8 also exposes uninitialized buffer bytes.**
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:3:The most consequential false premise is Q3’s description of #504. Its actual `lin_b is fg` assertion expects `FG_VAL = 0x77665544`, **not** the pre-paint `0x11111111`. The declined source GET preserves the caller’s foreground value, which the subsequent PUT writes. The probe explicitly rejects preserving the destination as a different disposition. This follows both the [executed assertion](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sgi_re_randompixel_probe.py:237) and the [caller’s initialization and GET](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:874). Thus #504 warrants the latch-and-return idiom; it does **not** supply the claimed unchanged-destination oracle.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:34:Also, “silent write” needs qualification: [`fatal()` returns](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/debugmsg.c:384), but prints a diagnostic. The current write is diagnosed, without being declined.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:36:For Q3, **pre-paint equality is the correct PUT postcondition, but insufficient evidence of decline**. Random output prevents an exact assertion about the defective output; it does not prevent an exact assertion about the repaired behavior.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:44:- A silent decline, an unlatched diagnostic, or a warning suppressed through bit sharing.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:51:For a guest-memory detector, retain full-span pre-paint checks, surrounding sentinels, completion/liveness, supported controls, and exact diagnostic counts. Exercise every listed default colour against depths `1,2,4,8`, with the warning bit initially clear and already set. Read back after the repeated declined operation; a warning-count row alone does not establish repeated decline. The fork already records this exact gap in [`latch cond`](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gdrom_toclen_probe.py:391).
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_pass1_20260907.txt:57:The proposed row **“YCRCB, depth 4: destination equals pre-paint” stays green**, as do equivalent depth-4 rows for the other default colours. Depths `1`, `2`, and `8` instead fall through to the shared write. Because the repair removed the RNG assignments, this mutation writes untouched buffer contents; it breaks decline without restoring `random()`.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_deepseek.txt:36:READ/REASONED. The print is in PSCALEADJ’s write body and `fatal()` returns, so it reaches the transcript. On the fix the decline `break`s before the print, so 0 is the correct expectation. Under fall-through the print occurs once. The channel is real.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_deepseek.txt:44:A fall-through at **T1CTL** or **T1ICR** — announce the decline, then let the halfword land — passes all 82 rows.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\ollama_deepseek.txt:47:The decline count remains 1, and the host survives because the body only prints `HUH?` and does not exit. There is no readback row for T1CTL or T1ICR, so the landed write is invisible.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_oracle_20260907.txt:34:- A declined access, with the supposed pre-paint never successfully stored.
