regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\pass2_panel\kimi.txt:673:  - Test-first chain: `head_79cd12e.out` (7/7 original witness) → `prefix_repinned_RED.out` (committed binary, 7/8, red exactly on the new inverting row `lin_b is fg`) → post-fix 8/8. The 1×1→1×4 vacuity repair is documented in the probe itself (`probe.frozen.py:189-197`), and the height-not-width reasoning is sound: with x=0 and LIN_A's `ofs = x & 4095`, four rows hit the same byte, so the value oracle survives — confirmed by BASE showing `0x77665544`. Shipped probe == frozen probe (md5 1daecf60).
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_design_20260907.txt:1:**VERDICT: REVISE — choose DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE with a return before the PUT transfer. `sgirebufuninit` is not a prerequisite. Source reachability is supported; the rung-3 witness remains pending.**
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_design_20260907.txt:7:**Q1: A declined PUT need not leave anything defined in `buf`, provided nothing consumes it.** The helper itself owns the memory write. Its callers receive no buffer to transfer afterward. [PUT switch and transfer](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:284).
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_design_20260907.txt:20:The return declines this pixel write. The drawing loop continues, and earlier GET operations are not undone.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_design_20260907.txt:26:I nevertheless prefer it because preserving destination bytes avoids inventing pixel data, and a bounded diagnostic exposes why rendering was declined. Silent decline loses that attribution. ACCEPT or BACKED ACCEPT would require a justified representation; the raw GET fallback alone does not establish YCRCB packing or conversion semantics. IMPLEMENT needs more evidence than the header’s constant.
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_design_20260907.txt:36:- Elsewhere, PCC2 explicitly distinguishes already-served reads, which it accepts, from writes it declines. [Primitive decline](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:944), [backed DE accesses](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1001), [MTE exits](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:1328), [PCC2 precedent](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_pcc2.c:67).
regress\artifacts\sgirandomcolour\codex_design_20260907.txt:38:For this repair, latch **only the announcement**; decline every invocation. Use an independent bit in the device’s `warned` field and the explicit `(once)` marker. Sharing `SGIRE_W_BADMODE` would let an addressing failure suppress the colour diagnostic. `fatal()` itself prints without terminating or applying the `debug()` quiet-mode check. [Latch allocation](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c:123), [logging implementation](C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/debugmsg.c:365).
