regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:894:  Also for Q1(c): PSCALEADJ noig channel — measured real (3c: count went 0→1 under fall-through) ✓. And on the fix 0 is right: the session's only PSCALEADJ touch is the declined put h ✓. One wrinkle: op pscale (separate session) ALSO put h's PSCALEADJ 0x0303 — counts DECL=1. Under M_FALL_PSCALEADJ that session: dcl=1 ✓ stays green (announce kept) — consistent with 3c showing ONLY op pscale noig red ✓ measured.
regress\artifacts\pcc2widthkills\pass3_seats_20260903\kimi.txt:902:  Now, severity/verdict. The chain-closing criterion: "the chain closes on the first VALID pass finding zero floor breaches". I found two clean-sweep mutants in the clause-(d) fall-through enumeration (VECBASE, IPL) — the very shape this pass added rows for — plus two out-of-enumeration sweeps (len==2 at 11 arms; writeflag-drop at any arm). The len==2 and writeflag-drop are new SHAPES (Q2's ask). The VECBASE/IPL fall-throughs are IN-enumeration uncovered cells (Q1(a)'s ask) — the enumeration is NOT closed. Per the brief's own floor rule, this pass cannot be the closing pass as-is. But the repair pattern is proven (the four rows it added DO kill their mutants, measured), and the fix is mechanical: add rb vecbase-self (byte-set VECBASE, put h at VECBASE, read back) and hwr ipl noig (count "read-only PCCTWO_IPL" == 0 in the hwr ipl session) — two rows → 84. Optionally rows for the two new shapes. So: GO-WITH-CHANGES, not NO-GO: the product diff needs no change (the product code is fine; it's the DETECTOR that's incomplete), the measured record all verifies, and the missing rows are cheap and well-specified. Hmm — but is "GO-WITH-CHANGES" right when the floor question ("does a clean-sweep mutant exist in the clause-(d) enumeration") has answer YES? The brief's own closing rule: chain closes on first valid pass with zero floor breaches. This pass FOUND breaches (by inspection, not yet measured). So the pass as-shipped fails its own closure criterion → strictly NO-GO for closure, GO-WITH-CHANGES for the diff with the two rows added and re-measured. The verdict scale the user gave: GO / NO-GO / GO-WITH-CHANGES. I'll go GO-WITH-CHANGES with the explicit note that the floor question currently answers YES (two clean-sweep cells), so the chain does NOT close this pass; the changes are detector-only, four rows total if the two new shapes are also taken.
