regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\ollama_glm.txt:1:**VERDICT — MEMBER 3 (DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE): `*color` UNTOUCHED on a failed GET — delete `*color = random()` — and the caller SKIPS the dependent PUT via the same return-value change already proposed for the sibling `tileptr` arm. NO PREMISE IS WRONG: all four hold as far as this packet shows.**
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\ollama_glm.txt:18:**Q1** — From the quoted arm, the PUT side already declines silently (default ends in `return`, no access); the harm is concentrated on GET: fabricated data the caller then writes. Untouched alone = fg smear ("plausible-looking"); zero = obviously wrong but still written; only skip-PUT stops the write. The return change must reach **every** caller of `horrible_getputpixel()` — not checkable from the packet; settle with the caller list (grep anchor). Members 1/4/6 lose in a clause each: default must remain (see below); 4 is the measured defect; 6 has no warrant that hardware returns any substitute.
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\ollama_glm.txt:20:**Q2** — Not licenced from this packet. "re_linear_b[] exists and is written" establishes *state*, not *semantics*; tile size (`x>>12`), base (`0x80000000|…`) and the ofs mask are exactly what a second linear mode could differ in. Settling fact: one doc line for the second linear format's geometry (crmfbreg.h comment, or a transferred warrant from upstream/NetBSD) — then case 5 moves to MEMBER 7 in a later round. REASONED: the `& 0x7` mask admits 3, 6, 7 from undocumented register values, so the default arm needs a member even after case 5 is implemented — member 3 is that member.
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\ollama_deepseek.txt:5:REASONED: The only option that stops the bogus write is FAULT. Leaving `*color` untouched or zeroing it still lets the caller write wrong data (foreground or zero). Implementing LIN_B as LIN_A with `re_linear_b[]` is a guess; the packet explicitly warns against shipping invented behaviour without a measured delta or transferred warrant. Therefore the unhandled LIN_B mode should cause the device access to return ≤0, and `memory_rw.c` will dispatch `EXCEPTION_DBE`, aborting the loop before any dependent PUT.
