regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\codex.txt:3122:MEMBER 3: DECLINE + LATCHED ANNOUNCE; failed GET leaves `*color` unchanged, returns failure, and suppresses the dependent PUT.
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\codex.txt:3128:| `copy lin_a` | `0xaabbccdd`, including after a declined command |
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\codex.txt:3132:| `lin_b diag` | Exactly one targeted decline announcement containing `(once)` across repeated commands in the same instance |
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\codex.txt:3138:For this command-constant mode failure, validate the modes actually required by the selected operation **before its loops**, and decline the command. Use one shared unsupported-mode announcement with a fresh `d->warned` bit, once per instance; existing `SGIRE_W_UNMAP_RD/WR` bits belong to other diagnostics. Retain failure handling in the pixel helper. Additional measurements needed: zero dependent PUTs—unchanged RAM alone cannot prove that—and repeated multi-pixel commands plus a fresh instance to establish latch scope.
regress\artifacts\sgirandompixel\design_panel\codex.txt:3140:**Do not implement LIN_B by array substitution on this evidence alone.** Case 4 carries `TODO... probably not correct!`. The existing MTE path selects either array, but its `if (entry & 0x80000000)` checks validity and searches by page; case 4 indexes directly and forces validity. That is supporting evidence for symmetry, not a complete transferred warrant for DE translation. Before member 7, obtain a DE address/validity reference or hardware comparison using distinct A/B mappings. Also, the probe’s `setup` programs **only A**: merely changing its expected LIN_B result to `SRC_VAL` would be unjustified.
