codex
I found why the UART attempt could stay quiet: debugger byte writes use `NO_EXCEPTIONS`, and the memory layer skips this UART’s callback under that flag. The apparent write confirmation is therefore not evidence that UART state changed. There is also a separate saved keyboard-controller trace naming the LCA stub; its binary provenance needs qualification.
