tools/pipeline/ledger.json-32813-     "hold_question": "68 of 70 registered interrupt handlers in this fork do not terminate, so a non-terminating handler is clearly possible -- but for an UNIMPLEMENTED delivery path, is a latched decline (the guest silently loses every ISA interrupt, announced once) an acceptable disposition, or does losing interrupts invisibly make member 7 (IMPLEMENT) the only honest answer?",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json-32814-     "note": "[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]  DELIBERATE hold -- opus5 and fable5 are reserved entirely for the 2026-09-09 adjudication by standing owner directive, so this stage ran without a flagship seat.  Not a seat failure and not agreement.  QUESTION: 68 of 70 registered interrupt handlers in this fork do not terminate, so a non-terminating handler is clearly possible -- but for an UNIMPLEMENTED delivery path, is a latched decline (the guest silently loses every ISA interrupt, announced once) an acceptable disposition, or does losing interrupts invisibly make member 7 (IMPLEMENT) the only honest answer?"
